          "metric": "WMC",
          "direction": "down",
          "confidence": 0.8
        }
      ],
      "sketch": "Replace the class with a @dataclass:\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass\nclass Customer:\n    customer_id: int\n    name: str\n    email: str\n    tier: str = \"standard\"\n\n    def is_premium(self) -> bool:\n        return self.tier == \"premium\"\n```\n\nThe public attributes replace the getter methods, eliminating the need for separate accessor methods. The only remaining method (`is_premium`) uses the `tier` attribute, so the method-attribute graph now has a single component, driving LCOM4 toward 0. The DCC remains unchanged because no new internal class references are introduced."
