  "risk_notes": "Existing code that calls the getter methods (`customer_id()`, `name()`, etc.) will break; these calls must be updated to use the public attributes (`customer.customer_id`, `customer.name`, etc.). If the class is part of a public API, changing attribute visibility may affect external consumers. Additionally, if future behavior is added that requires encapsulation, the design may need to revert to explicit getters or property methods."
